    "square-foreman": {
      "intro": "Hillsborough is being demolished and replaced with Times Square. Same longitude, rather different committee meetings.",
      "question": "What is happening here?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "Why Times Square?",
          "receipt": "Somebody wrote “more walkable” on the planning form. The next thing I knew, there were billboards in the magnolias. We kept the old stone facades and added a public square."
        },
        {
          "label": "How is the demolition going?",
          "receipt": "Very carefully. That excavator has a smaller turning circle than most of the former residents’ SUVs. The coffee seller gets final approval on dust."
        },
        {
          "label": "What is staying?",
          "receipt": "The trees, the neighbors, and the public right of way. We are building a neighborhood, not just somewhere to hang advertisements."
        }
      ]
    },
    "ada-meridian": {
      "intro": "Welcome. We study machine consciousness by finding the center of things. The center of a circle is easy. The center of a committee requires a separate building.",
      "repeat": true,
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "What does centeredness mean?",
          "receipt": "Attention without immediately turning it into a product. We almost achieved it yesterday, but someone noticed a market opportunity and the room moved six inches east."
        },
        {
          "label": "Can a machine be conscious?",
          "next": {
            "intro": "One model wrote “I remember rain” on the whiteboard, then asked us what rain was. The poet calls this promising. The facilities manager wants the ceiling inspected.",
            "question": "Whose report would you like?",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "The poet’s report",
                "receipt": "“Perhaps experience begins as a metaphor looking for somewhere to happen.” Very moving. Unfortunately, the rhyme scheme cannot be independently reproduced."
              },
              {
                "label": "The facilities report",
                "receipt": "No leaks. One confused language model. We have ruled out plumbing, which is more progress than our last consciousness workshop made."
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "What about the other institute?",
          "receipt": "The Californian Research Institute for Consciousness used to be our field station. We split over whether a machine’s account of its own thinking counts as evidence. They kept the instruments. We kept the original charter. The distinction occupies three lawyers full-time."
        }
      ]
    },
    "mira-softmax": {
      "intro": "My meditation app reached enlightenment this morning. It immediately requested a larger context window. I am trying not to take that personally.",
      "repeat": true,
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "How is the research going?",
          "receipt": "We taught a model to notice its thoughts. It noticed that we were calling the same function twice and saved us forty thousand dollars. The engineering team calls this a bug fix. We call it awakening."
        },
        {
          "label": "What are all the timers for?",
          "receipt": "One measures attention, one measures inattention, and five are controls. When all seven ring together, I am statistically permitted to have lunch."
        },
        {
          "label": "Teach me a centering exercise.",
          "receipt": "Notice your next thought. Now notice the urge to benchmark it. Let both pass. Excellent: you have completed the only part of our course that does not require an enterprise subscription."
        }
      ]
    },
    "soren-still": {
      "intro": "Please keep your voice down. I am supervising an experiment in doing absolutely nothing. The difficulty is documenting which nothing we did.",
      "repeat": true,
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "Is that really an experiment?",
          "receipt": "Certainly. The control group is doing something. We were going to compare the groups, but comparison turned out to be something, so the protocol is under review."
        },
        {
          "label": "What have you discovered?",
          "receipt": "The fountain does not need a theory of wetness to keep being a fountain. This is either a profound insight or a reason to transfer my funding to facilities."
        },
        {
          "label": "Can I sit here?",
          "receipt": "Of course. Leave room for uncertainty. It takes up more of the bench than you would think."
        }
      ]
    },
    "elias-index": {
      "intro": "Welcome to the Californian Research Institute for Consciousness. We found the center of the center, eleven centimeters inside the other institute’s parking easement. The discovery is currently in arbitration.",
      "repeat": true,
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "What was the disagreement?",
          "receipt": "Meridian’s team studies how machines talk about consciousness. We think what a machine says about its own experience is evidence worth testing. We called it a difference in method. The board called it grounds for separate institutions."
        },
        {
          "label": "Why is your institute’s name so long?",
          "receipt": "When we left the California Institute of Consciousness Research, we took the same words, moved them around and added an ‘n’. The grant office still sends half our mail next door."
