  "tweet_1972486813727244511_1": {
    "id": "tweet_1972486813727244511_1",
    "title": "So I think Mayor Lurie's been doing a good job.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["1972486813727244511.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "So I think Mayor Lurie's been doing a good job.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Yeah hundred percent except the speeding cameras. You hear about this shit?",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "No, all I know is that during Covid, SF dropped its traffic law enforcement to zero.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Well now they got these speeding cameras all over town and I'm getting all these tickets or whatever.",
        "next": "line-5"
      },
      "line-5": { "id": "line-5", "speaker": "player", "text": "Uh-huh.", "next": "line-6" },
      "line-6": {
        "id": "line-6",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Yeah they added all these speed limits everywhere too it's bullshit man. Now everything's a 20 mile an hour zone and if I'm going 31 in a 20 I'm gonna get fined fifty fucking bucks? Fucking bullshit.",
        "next": "line-7"
      },
      "line-7": {
        "id": "line-7",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Uh-huh yeah that's crazy. [internally: YES! YES! STRAIGHT INTO MY VEINS! AHHHH!]",
        "next": "line-8"
      },
      "line-8": {
        "id": "line-8",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Yeah I got 7 of these damn things already.",
        "next": "line-9"
      },
      "line-9": {
        "id": "line-9",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Wow no way. [internally: I am so happy.]",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_1993542360949833919_1": {
    "id": "tweet_1993542360949833919_1",
    "title": "An interesting thing about tech vs. finance is how much cultural power founde...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["1993542360949833919.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "An interesting thing about tech vs. finance is how much cultural power founders have.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "You could pull $10M/year at Citadel or DE Shaw and ~nobody would know who you are.",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Founders? You can pull zero revenue but post about the dream of greatness to achieve moderate celebrity status.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "There's something romantic here, come to think of it. Founders do not necessarily have to achieve the big numbers.",
        "next": "line-5"
      },
      "line-5": {
        "id": "line-5",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "They can still win respect just by trying their best and inspiring others. The courage of the man in the arena is to be admired.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_1994567789831754175_1": {
    "id": "tweet_1994567789831754175_1",
    "title": "Sometimes I think about gun control: from about 2010 to 2015 it felt like thi...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["1994567789831754175.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Sometimes I think about gun control: from about 2010 to 2015 it felt like this was the dominant issue in US politics.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "And I wonder whether this was a mistake from the mainstream dems -- too contentious an issue with too little payoff.",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "It was probably clear from the start that gun control proponents could never achieve a sufficient majority to enact real change.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Let alone the obvious practical impossibility of carrying out gun control in a country with several hundred million guns in circulation.",
        "next": "line-5"
      },
      "line-5": {
        "id": "line-5",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "At the same time, it alienated a ton of conservative voters and drove a deep demographic/ideological divide.",
        "next": "line-6"
      },
      "line-6": {
        "id": "line-6",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "It would've been possible to drive change on bipartisan issues that wouldn't have contributed to polarization.",
        "next": "line-7"
      },
      "line-7": {
        "id": "line-7",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "In retrospect, it all looks like a strategic misfire, an overextension and overspend of political capital on something that never carried true popular appeal.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_1999547741287121405_1": {
    "id": "tweet_1999547741287121405_1",
    "title": "It's funny how dated ~2015 startup culture feels now. \"We have beer on tap! W...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["1999547741287121405.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It's funny how dated ~2015 startup culture feels now. \"We have beer on tap! We're a fun company!\"",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Today there are no startups with beer on tap. To most young engineers, the idea of even drinking alcohol in general seems strange and suboptimal.",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I haven't seen a ping-pong table in an office in years.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "A lot of current startup culture is highly performative -- virtually none of the people who claim to work 996 actually do, most of the office bunk beds are never used, etc. But the culture is still a lot more ambitious and concrete than it was ten years ago.",
        "next": "line-5"
      },
      "line-5": {
        "id": "line-5",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "There was a lot of woo-ish bullshit in the early 2010s. Companies had ambitions to change the world, but with stuff like a Yoga-Centric Social Network or Cat-Sitting Apps.",
        "next": "line-6"
      },
      "line-6": {
        "id": "line-6",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "This crop of startups seems to have died out and been replaced with a much more hardcore and optimized views -- laser-focused on big TAMs, shifting economic value from labor to technology, and summoning the Machine God.",
        "next": "line-7"
      },
      "line-7": {
        "id": "line-7",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "It may feel like there's a lot of startup grift these days -- and there is -- but that's just because of the sheer size of the ecosystem now. Some of the froth bubbles over.",
        "next": "line-8"
      },
      "line-8": {
        "id": "line-8",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "But on a whole it feels far more serious, ambitious, and actually world-changing than when I arrived ten years ago. Silicon Valley is out of its teenage years and in adulthood now.",
        "next": "line-9"
      },
      "line-9": {
        "id": "line-9",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "There's probably some extent to which this is a washing out of the \"tech weirdo\" culture, and a replacement by a more professionalized culture.",
        "next": "line-10"
      },
      "line-10": {
        "id": "line-10",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Tech today is no longer as Burning Man adjacent, fewer engineers are misfits elsewhere, and it's also less accessible to bootcamps and the like.",
        "next": "line-11"
      },
      "line-11": {
        "id": "line-11",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Product Managers today would've been Investment Bankers 15 years ago. It's like a game where the metagame has slowly become figured out, and what was once fringe is now mainstream.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2004960386693693525_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2004960386693693525_1",
    "title": "On the wealth tax: you should be *extremely worried* that California is runni...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2004960386693693525.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "On the wealth tax: you should be *extremely worried* that California is running record budget deficits during the *good part* of the economic cycle.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
