  "tweet_2048490877056888951_15": {
    "id": "tweet_2048490877056888951_15",
    "title": "Sometimes I hear founders and execs make excuses for the state of their busin...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2048490877056888951.txt"],
    "start": "line-52",
    "nodes": {
      "line-52": {
        "id": "line-52",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Sometimes I hear founders and execs make excuses for the state of their business: \"Our net dollar retention has always been 120% but we're down to 90% now because of this one-off issue with our biggest customer --\" yeah OK your NDR is 90% not 120%.",
        "next": "line-53"
      },
      "line-53": {
        "id": "line-53",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Everyone, literally everyone, has this stuff happen to them. This is baked into how people evaluate these metrics.",
        "next": "line-54"
      },
      "line-54": {
        "id": "line-54",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "No excuses or special cases!",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2048490877056888951_16": {
    "id": "tweet_2048490877056888951_16",
    "title": "Nostalgia is big business. People pay through the nose for Disney experiences...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2048490877056888951.txt"],
    "start": "line-56",
    "nodes": {
      "line-56": {
        "id": "line-56",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Nostalgia is big business. People pay through the nose for Disney experiences, rare Pokemon cards, you name it.",
        "next": "line-57"
      },
      "line-57": {
        "id": "line-57",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Even seeing washed-up artists from thirty years ago.",
        "next": "line-58"
      },
      "line-58": {
        "id": "line-58",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It's a little sad, of course, to see people spend endlessly to try to relive memories or feelings that can never be felt again.",
        "next": "line-59"
      },
      "line-59": {
        "id": "line-59",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "This suggests that people's preferences really get set fairly early in childhood, maybe around the teens, and then that's it for life.",
        "next": "line-60"
      },
      "line-60": {
        "id": "line-60",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "What that means is kind of interesting. The big businesses of the future will invest heavily to own the warm fuzzy feelings of childhood that will then create nostalgia-driven consumers for decades.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2049549461391847647_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2049549461391847647_1",
    "title": "Sometimes, an acquaintance will reach out to me to \"catch up\" casually. There...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2049549461391847647.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Sometimes, an acquaintance will reach out to me to \"catch up\" casually. There's nothing I like more than a nice wide-ranging conversation with no agenda, so I usually say yes.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Then, 30 or 45 minutes in, they try to be very sneaky about this, they bring up -- oh-just-by-the-way -- some commercial request: an intro to so-and-so, maybe I'll consider buying their product, funding their company, whatever, and it's so disappointing...",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "The last half hour was a fake conversation, a plying motion to prepare for some sale, none of the personal interest was real.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "I understand that there's a certain school of thought in favor of doing this, but I don't like it at all.",
        "next": "line-5"
      },
      "line-5": {
        "id": "line-5",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "I much prefer when people reach out straightforwardly with their commercial request and none of the social fakery or time waste.",
        "next": "line-6"
      },
      "line-6": {
        "id": "line-6",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I like doing the inversion: \"Hey can you help with X?\" and then afterwards ask to catch up.",
        "next": "line-7"
      },
      "line-7": {
        "id": "line-7",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "That's the way to do it.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2052046002912395409_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2052046002912395409_1",
    "title": "I can't stop thinking about the LA copper wire thefts.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2052046002912395409.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I can't stop thinking about the LA copper wire thefts.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "For background: in LA, thieves have been stripping streetlights of their electrical wiring and selling it for scrap.",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It is amazingly destructive: for every $1 of wire they sell, the city has to spend $100-$1000 on repairs.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Literally, the thief might make a couple hundred bucks, and the city has to spend six figures.",
        "next": "line-5"
      },
      "line-5": {
        "id": "line-5",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Yes and the streetlights are out, which may lead to traffic accidents or other problems. It's an extremely antisocial crime.",
        "next": "line-6"
      },
      "line-6": {
        "id": "line-6",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Astoundingly, the city seems unwilling to do something about this. A guy invented a better way to lock down streetlights -- they didn't want it. The idea of \"look for the thieves and put them in jail\" has been unpopular for reasons unclear to me.",
        "next": "line-7"
      },
      "line-7": {
        "id": "line-7",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Proposed solutions, like making scrap yards record who sold them copper wiring, seem ineffective.",
        "next": "line-8"
      },
      "line-8": {
        "id": "line-8",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "The most cynical explanation for this is that the incentives lead to crime.",
        "next": "line-9"
      },
      "line-9": {
        "id": "line-9",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Right. The money spent on repairs is primarily spent on local union labor. For them, this is great. There's a whole industry for servicing these problems.",
        "next": "line-10"
      },
      "line-10": {
        "id": "line-10",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "And the city gets to say that it is working on fixing the issues.",
        "next": "line-11"
      },
      "line-11": {
        "id": "line-11",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Up to some limit, the more of these issues, the better.",
        "next": "line-12"
      },
      "line-12": {
        "id": "line-12",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Everybody wins: the thieves win, the laborers win, the repair industry wins, certain politicians and candidates win. Well, the actual resident, the taxpayer -- they lose, but what are you gonna do?",
        "next": "line-13"
      },
      "line-13": {
        "id": "line-13",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Live with the lights off? Vote for the tough-on-crime candidate? Unthinkable.",
        "next": "line-14"
      },
      "line-14": {
        "id": "line-14",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "You can look at this as a system that has degenerated into being a recursive loop that drains the resources of its citizens.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2057490142756221296_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2057490142756221296_1",
