  "tweet_2066804703921393850_20": {
    "id": "tweet_2066804703921393850_20",
    "title": "Public markets and accredited investor laws interact in interesting ways.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2066804703921393850.txt"],
    "start": "line-79",
    "nodes": {
      "line-79": {
        "id": "line-79",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Public markets and accredited investor laws interact in interesting ways.",
        "next": "line-80"
      },
      "line-80": {
        "id": "line-80",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Public markets were regulated to protect retail investors with laws on what financial data must be reported, what accounting standards are acceptable, and so on.",
        "next": "line-81"
      },
      "line-81": {
        "id": "line-81",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "This proved too onerous, so companies stayed private longer.",
        "next": "line-82"
      },
      "line-82": {
        "id": "line-82",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "But retail investors still want access, so some people want to shred the accredited investor laws altogether.",
        "next": "line-83"
      },
      "line-83": {
        "id": "line-83",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "But that seems like the worst of both worlds: the opacity and pay-to-play of private markets, mixed with the lack of common standards and regulatory watchdogs of public markets.",
        "next": "line-84"
      },
      "line-84": {
        "id": "line-84",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "I'm sure that retail would largely lose money, as they did in crypto.",
        "next": "line-85"
      },
      "line-85": {
        "id": "line-85",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "To resolve this tension, I think the right solution is to make it easy for private companies to go public earlier.",
        "next": "line-86"
      },
      "line-86": {
        "id": "line-86",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "That's much better for the public and for the economy than removing accreditation laws.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2066804703921393850_21": {
    "id": "tweet_2066804703921393850_21",
    "title": "Exile is a punishment that no longer exists in our well-partitioned world.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2066804703921393850.txt"],
    "start": "line-88",
    "nodes": {
      "line-88": {
        "id": "line-88",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Exile is a punishment that no longer exists in our well-partitioned world.",
        "next": "line-89"
      },
      "line-89": {
        "id": "line-89",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It was a very powerful concept because it conveys \"we don't want to kill you, but you cannot impose costs on us any longer\".",
        "next": "line-90"
      },
      "line-90": {
        "id": "line-90",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "It's interesting because there are a lot of people today in that position, but we have no adequate legal/judicial response.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2069441547301691547_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2069441547301691547_1",
    "title": "One thing that's weird about your 30s is that you'll see some people, whom yo...",
