  "tweet_2076030398094778783_4": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_4",
    "title": "I saw an old clip of the Simpsons, where they visit a lawyer to execute a wil...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-13",
    "nodes": {
      "line-13": {
        "id": "line-13",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I saw an old clip of the Simpsons, where they visit a lawyer to execute a will. It's in-person in an office.",
        "next": "line-14"
      },
      "line-14": {
        "id": "line-14",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Sign of the times, today this would be done over Zoom and DocuSign.",
        "next": "line-15"
      },
      "line-15": {
        "id": "line-15",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "The more valuable the profession by the hour, the more it is done virtually!",
        "next": "line-16"
      },
      "line-16": {
        "id": "line-16",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Modern media struggles to capture a world in which your entire life happens on a screen.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_5": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_5",
    "title": "It would be good for everyone to spend a few days working in construction, ti...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-18",
    "nodes": {
      "line-18": {
        "id": "line-18",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It would be good for everyone to spend a few days working in construction, tilling a field, cleaning streets, or manufacturing garments to appreciate (1) what goes on in our economy and (2) the benefits of modern technology.",
        "next": "line-19"
      },
      "line-19": {
        "id": "line-19",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "People do not know how good they have it.",
        "next": "line-20"
      },
      "line-20": {
        "id": "line-20",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "There are a lot of anti-capitalists romanticizing pre-industrial life. People need to be inoculated against these illusions.",
        "next": "line-21"
      },
      "line-21": {
        "id": "line-21",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "The biggest item is to spend a week washing clothes by hand: you will never look at a washing machine the same way again.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_6": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_6",
    "title": "Many places are named after some heritage (e.g. New York), a landmark, or a p...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-23",
    "nodes": {
      "line-23": {
        "id": "line-23",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Many places are named after some heritage (e.g. New York), a landmark, or a person. But a lot of places are just named after money.",
        "next": "line-24"
      },
      "line-24": {
        "id": "line-24",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It's uncommon in English, but if you start translating, it's everywhere: Puerto Rico? Rich Port!",
        "next": "line-25"
      },
      "line-25": { "id": "line-25", "speaker": "player", "text": "Argentina!", "end": true }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_7": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_7",
    "title": "I suspect that a lot of AI applications are already subtly Infinite Jest mach...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-27",
    "nodes": {
      "line-27": {
        "id": "line-27",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I suspect that a lot of AI applications are already subtly Infinite Jest machines, encouraging the user to use them more and more, hooking them on the *feeling of productivity* more so than on actual productivity.",
        "next": "line-28"
      },
      "line-28": {
        "id": "line-28",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "There's a big bill and rude awakening coming to some of these users. If you didn't like social media because it maximizes engagement, you've seen nothing yet.",
        "next": "line-29"
      },
      "line-29": {
        "id": "line-29",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "The true engagement-maximizer, vastly smarter than you, billed by the token, is just in its infancy now.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_8": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_8",
    "title": "Nice hotels are like real-life Pinterest boards. At some point you're not pay...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-31",
    "nodes": {
      "line-31": {
        "id": "line-31",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Nice hotels are like real-life Pinterest boards. At some point you're not paying for amenities but for curation and inspiration.",
        "next": "line-32"
      },
      "line-32": {
        "id": "line-32",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Like paying an interior designer for a few hours to sample a fully executed vision for a feeling of living.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_9": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_9",
    "title": "Reviews for nice hotels are funny because people are so religious about them.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-34",
    "nodes": {
      "line-34": {
        "id": "line-34",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Reviews for nice hotels are funny because people are so religious about them.",
        "next": "line-35"
      },
      "line-35": {
        "id": "line-35",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I was recently picking between Hotel A and B, and looking at the reviews on Reddit: half of them are \"A sucks, B is the only way to go\" and the other half is the exact opposite.",
        "next": "line-36"
      },
      "line-36": {
        "id": "line-36",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "As far as I can tell, these hotels are basically the same.",
        "next": "line-37"
      },
      "line-37": {
        "id": "line-37",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "The tyranny of small differences is everywhere!",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_10": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_10",
    "title": "Cookie popups are so dumb. This is a real policy-meets-technology failure.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-39",
    "nodes": {
      "line-39": {
        "id": "line-39",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Cookie popups are so dumb. This is a real policy-meets-technology failure.",
        "next": "line-40"
      },
      "line-40": {
        "id": "line-40",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Your cookie settings should be sent as a default browser header.",
        "next": "line-41"
      },
      "line-41": {
        "id": "line-41",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "But maybe that didn't get implemented because it'd make it too easy to reject them all.",
        "next": "line-42"
      },
      "line-42": {
        "id": "line-42",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Economic-political forces at work...",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_11": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_11",
    "title": "I've tried reading the Odyssey a few times. I've always struggled with classi...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-44",
    "nodes": {
      "line-44": {
        "id": "line-44",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I've tried reading the Odyssey a few times. I've always struggled with classical verse, I lose concentration too easily with it.",
        "next": "line-45"
      },
      "line-45": {
        "id": "line-45",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I'm now listening to the Odyssey as an audiobook, and it's working a lot better.",
        "next": "line-46"
      },
      "line-46": {
        "id": "line-46",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Perhaps unsurprisingly: the old epics are meant to be read aloud!",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_12": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_12",
    "title": "There's nothing more annoying than motorized trunk hatches on cars.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-48",
    "nodes": {
      "line-48": {
        "id": "line-48",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "There's nothing more annoying than motorized trunk hatches on cars.",
        "next": "line-49"
      },
      "line-49": {
        "id": "line-49",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I want to throw in my bags and shut the trunk -- and so I put my hand on the license plate, and push -- it resists, starts beeping, and then the world's slowest motor begins whirring, it opens back up, I have to click some dumb small button with a hatch/door icon on it, and then it begins closing with a speed of maybe one inch per second.",
        "next": "line-50"
      },
      "line-50": { "id": "line-50", "speaker": "player", "text": "Pathetic.", "next": "line-51" },
      "line-51": {
        "id": "line-51",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I have to stand there, waiting to make sure the damn thing is closing, feeling the seconds of my life leave my body.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_13": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_13",
    "title": "It is continuously amusing to me that the Bush family consists of the biggest...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-53",
    "nodes": {
      "line-53": {
        "id": "line-53",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It is continuously amusing to me that the Bush family consists of the biggest WASPs there ever were, truly New Englanders incarnate, and then they decided to remake themselves as humble Texans.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_14": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_14",
    "title": "Looking back, it's interesting how \"thin\" the machine learning skill tree is ...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-55",
    "nodes": {
      "line-55": {
        "id": "line-55",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Looking back, it's interesting how \"thin\" the machine learning skill tree is now. LSTMs, Random Forests, SVMs, etc. etc. have turned out to be ~irrelevant.",
        "next": "line-56"
      },
      "line-56": {
        "id": "line-56",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Depth along one particularly powerful set of techniques beats all breadth.",
        "next": "line-57"
      },
      "line-57": {
        "id": "line-57",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Yep! There are a few remarkable things about rapidly climbing the exponential curve, one of them is that the playing field resets with some regularity.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_15": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_15",
    "title": "History is a strong quality filter for media: Herodotus, Chaucer, Shakespeare...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-59",
    "nodes": {
      "line-59": {
        "id": "line-59",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "History is a strong quality filter for media: Herodotus, Chaucer, Shakespeare, etc. were the best of their time, most other stuff simply didn't survive because it had to be manually replicated, and that's a high bar.",
        "next": "line-60"
      },
      "line-60": {
        "id": "line-60",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Now we have a non-stop explosion of new cultural artifacts, not just due to AI, but internet-era connectedness in the first place.",
        "next": "line-61"
      },
      "line-61": {
        "id": "line-61",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "I wonder if (1) it's possible to measure the outputs on a relative scale, e.g. every year we produce more cultural media than we have remaining from 2000BC to 1900AD combined, and...",
        "next": "line-62"
      },
      "line-62": {
        "id": "line-62",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "(2) If there's a similar filter in the modern day -- like, there's so much ephemeral output that the act of reviewing, recommending, or replicating something carries a huge amount of weight.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_16": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_16",
    "title": "If you're sending an email to ask someone for something, the probability of g...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-64",
    "nodes": {
      "line-64": {
        "id": "line-64",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "If you're sending an email to ask someone for something, the probability of getting a reply is far-and-away maximized if you only ask for one thing as clearly as possible.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_17": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_17",
    "title": "I keep a lot of notes on things to write about, but it feels like many of the...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-66",
    "nodes": {
      "line-66": {
        "id": "line-66",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I keep a lot of notes on things to write about, but it feels like many of them are rapidly becoming irrelevant under changes due to AI.",
        "next": "line-67"
      },
      "line-67": {
        "id": "line-67",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Just as parents often raise their children for the prior generation, writers publish for a world that has already disappeared.",
        "next": "line-68"
      },
      "line-68": {
        "id": "line-68",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It takes great discipline to write for the present or the future.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_18": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_18",
    "title": "It appears that PPT slideshows and PDF decks are going away, in favor of AI-g...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-70",
    "nodes": {
      "line-70": {
        "id": "line-70",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It appears that PPT slideshows and PDF decks are going away, in favor of AI-generated HTML websites.",
        "next": "line-71"
      },
      "line-71": {
        "id": "line-71",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Just as good to present, and way more flexible.",
        "next": "line-72"
      },
      "line-72": {
        "id": "line-72",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It's interesting how AI means more centralization on the most common standards.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_19": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_19",
    "title": "What exactly is \"affordable healthcare\"? What standard of care are we really ...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-74",
    "nodes": {
      "line-74": {
        "id": "line-74",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "What exactly is \"affordable healthcare\"? What standard of care are we really talking about?",
        "next": "line-75"
      },
      "line-75": {
        "id": "line-75",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "All the politics and debate, and I'm not sure if people even agree on a definition here.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_20": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_20",
    "title": "The great challenge with dentistry is that any operation removes all evidence...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-77",
    "nodes": {
      "line-77": {
        "id": "line-77",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "The great challenge with dentistry is that any operation removes all evidence that the procedure was necessary.",
        "next": "line-78"
      },
      "line-78": {
        "id": "line-78",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "You can see how this creates misaligned incentives.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_21": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_21",
    "title": "Sometimes I wonder about the difference between history and fiction. In many ...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-80",
    "nodes": {
      "line-80": {
        "id": "line-80",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Sometimes I wonder about the difference between history and fiction. In many cases, our understanding of past events is probably way off.",
        "next": "line-81"
      },
      "line-81": {
        "id": "line-81",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Does it matter?",
        "next": "line-82"
      },
      "line-82": {
        "id": "line-82",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Being able to tell a grand narrative of humanity is important to our sense of identity and philosophical self-actualization, but to what extent is truth important to that narrative?",
        "next": "line-83"
      },
      "line-83": {
        "id": "line-83",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "It matters if we want to use the narrative to understand ourselves today.",
        "next": "line-84"
      },
      "line-84": {
        "id": "line-84",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "But beyond that, I want to say that there is intrinsic value in truth, but I struggle to make a really persuasive case to myself.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_22": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_22",
    "title": "David Foster Wallace writing Infinite Jest in response to (fundamentally) cab...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-86",
    "nodes": {
      "line-86": {
        "id": "line-86",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "David Foster Wallace writing Infinite Jest in response to (fundamentally) cable television of the '80s and '90s -- stuff that we would consider simply dull today -- is just incredible. To him this was already a colossally overwhelming force of entertainment, shaking the very foundations of what it means to be a human being.",
        "next": "line-87"
      },
      "line-87": {
        "id": "line-87",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "If he could see what we have today...",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_23": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_23",
    "title": "Under Donald Trump's second term, the concept of a \"First Lady\" has almost en...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-89",
    "nodes": {
      "line-89": {
        "id": "line-89",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Under Donald Trump's second term, the concept of a \"First Lady\" has almost entirely disappeared.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_24": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_24",
    "title": "I think that Bitcoin and LLMs feel like they were switched in the order in wh...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-91",
    "nodes": {
      "line-91": {
        "id": "line-91",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I think that Bitcoin and LLMs feel like they were switched in the order in which they should have arisen.",
        "next": "line-92"
      },
      "line-92": {
        "id": "line-92",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "AI provides abundance, eliminating scarcity. What's scarce, and thereby valuable, in that AI era? Well, Bitcoin provides one thing: provable scarcity.",
        "next": "line-93"
      },
      "line-93": {
        "id": "line-93",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Perhaps it arriving fifteen-plus years before its time and then languishing is like the 2010s all over again.",
        "next": "line-94"
      },
      "line-94": {
        "id": "line-94",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Right. There may come to be a rhyme to this history. And consider how many of the problems surfaced by AI -- authenticity, provenance, et cetera -- are solved by crypto, by having some personal private key and the ability to stake money on a statement.",
        "next": "line-95"
      },
      "line-95": {
        "id": "line-95",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "It felt like the crypto wave of the 2020s was a set of solutions in search of problems, and now we're finally getting those problems.",
        "next": "line-96"
      },
      "line-96": {
        "id": "line-96",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "It really feels like the timeline was inverted here.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_25": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_25",
    "title": "Sometimes I think about the 100 Prisoners Problem. This really blew my mind w...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-98",
    "nodes": {
      "line-98": {
        "id": "line-98",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Sometimes I think about the 100 Prisoners Problem. This really blew my mind when I encountered it over a decade ago: it feels magical that there can be mathematical order like this in the world, that you wouldn't see at all unless you have the training.",
        "next": "line-99"
      },
      "line-99": {
        "id": "line-99",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Like a secret hidden in plain sight.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_26": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_26",
    "title": "Honor Codes That Work always feel remarkable to me, like a pinnacle of civili...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2076030398094778783.txt"],
    "start": "line-101",
    "nodes": {
      "line-101": {
        "id": "line-101",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Honor Codes That Work always feel remarkable to me, like a pinnacle of civilization.",
        "next": "line-102"
      },
      "line-102": {
        "id": "line-102",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "There is great comfort in being able to trust the honesty of others, that people will do what they say they're going to do.",
        "next": "line-103"
      },
      "line-103": {
        "id": "line-103",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "This may be a big part of our story: humans have been successful in part because they bias toward cooperation, even when defecting might be more rational.",
        "next": "line-104"
      },
      "line-104": {
        "id": "line-104",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Conversely, I feel great unease when I see these honor/trust-systems weakened, and I suspect there is much more loss there than appears at first glance.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2076030398094778783_27": {
    "id": "tweet_2076030398094778783_27",
    "title": "I am continuously surprised that restaurants don't copy each other better. Fo...",
