  "tweet_2089894747834094067_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2089894747834094067_1",
    "title": "As a child, my mother would tell me the classic German saying \"If you have ne...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2089894747834094067.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "As a child, my mother would tell me the classic German saying \"If you have never eaten cake in bed, you do not know how much crumbs poke you.\"",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "This was always presented to me as literal advice about not eating snacks in bed, but it has finally dawned on me that this is a metaphor.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2093158351555506649_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2093158351555506649_1",
    "title": "Let me tell you about my morning in San Francisco.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2093158351555506649.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Let me tell you about my morning in San Francisco.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I wake up. Normally I take a Waymo downtown, but today I walk over to Golden Gate Park.",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Early in the morning, before 8:00, the park is bathed in a heavy fog. The mist hangs in the air and you can feel it on your cheeks as you walk.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "The park is hilly and thick with green of the grass and the trees. The birds chirp from far out of sight. In that moment, the world feels still. The dew will leave your sneakers wet if you walk across the meadows. Backpack on, walking up a slight incline in the grey and green, feels like you might be climbing up a misty mountain top somewhere far away.",
        "next": "line-5"
      },
      "line-5": {
        "id": "line-5",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I walk all the way through the park to its very south-eastern corner, and keep walking east through Cole Valley.",
        "next": "line-6"
      },
      "line-6": {
        "id": "line-6",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "The fog quickly ends there, from one block to the next, and some of the most picturesque Victorians in the city have their colors revealed by the soft sunlight. In the center of Cole Valley is a cafe called Wooden Coffeehouse that has the most comfortable, finely curved handmade wooden chairs in the city.",
        "next": "line-7"
      },
      "line-7": {
        "id": "line-7",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I purchase a cappuccino, which is rich and creamy, and I think about how much I love being there.",
        "next": "line-8"
      },
      "line-8": {
        "id": "line-8",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Across the street is a streetcar stop. It moves quickly and smoothly and carves its way straight through the hills in the center of the city.",
        "next": "line-9"
      },
      "line-9": {
        "id": "line-9",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "When it drops me off at my workplace among all the high-rises downtown, there's not a drop of fog in the air, just the pure great sun of California that I had been told about and imagined long before I first arrived here.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2096810545672315273_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2096810545672315273_1",
    "title": "(1) Akira and (2) Infinite Jest are similar in how it feels like the author w...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2096810545672315273.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "(1) Akira and (2) Infinite Jest are similar in how it feels like the author wanted to write a cool story about (1) motorcycles/sci-fi Tokyo and (2) tennis/drugs, but just couldn't resist the call of (1) supernatural nuclear armageddon and (2) people's relationship to entertainment.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2096975657423024151_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2096975657423024151_1",
    "title": "Oh by the way.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2096975657423024151.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": { "id": "line-1", "speaker": "npc", "text": "Oh by the way.", "next": "line-2" },
      "line-2": { "id": "line-2", "speaker": "player", "text": "Yes?", "next": "line-3" },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "If you believe in a \"permanent underclass\", it should be obvious that there will be no overclass.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "In the face of an arbitrarily expanding power differential, you being an \"owner\" of Class B Common Stock in The Last Company will be short-lived, and in retrospect, naive.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2102575499293966821_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2102575499293966821_1",
    "title": "I've been thinking a lot about AI disintermediating human relationships. This...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2102575499293966821.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I've been thinking a lot about AI disintermediating human relationships. This seems like a real challenge to me, and I'm not sure how to feel about it.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Thanks to AI, in the long run there will be no need for me to ask anyone else for help with anything, and consequently, there will be no opportunity for people to feel useful and appreciated when they provide a service.",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "That give-and-take between people is the core of our social fabric.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "And it has already been fraying for a long time, even pre-AI.",
        "next": "line-5"
      },
      "line-5": {
        "id": "line-5",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Many optimists say things like \"AI will automate all the rote work so people can focus on their passions and being together\" -- but there is no \"being together\" without some shared struggle or objective.",
        "next": "line-6"
      },
      "line-6": {
        "id": "line-6",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "There is no building trust without need -- and in an AI-induced age of abundance, there may just not be any need.",
        "next": "line-7"
      },
      "line-7": {
        "id": "line-7",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Social fabric is woven by countless daily small, necessary interactions with other people -- and those interactions may simply go away because your AI agent of choice ends up being your interface to the world around yourself.",
        "next": "line-8"
      },
      "line-8": {
        "id": "line-8",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Not because of any shortcoming, like being lazy or complacent, but because AI will be a better interface.",
        "next": "line-9"
      },
      "line-9": {
        "id": "line-9",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Why ask your friend for advice when AI will be more patient, less judgmental, and understand you better? What's left for parents to teach their children if AI is a better tutor in all respects? And so forth.",
        "next": "line-10"
      },
      "line-10": {
        "id": "line-10",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Many incipient changes or risks due to AI do not worry me much. I am very optimistic about what AI can bring to our future. But this one challenge bothers me; it seems like it could spell a fundamental reorganization of our society, isolating the individual much more greatly than ever before.",
        "next": "line-11"
      },
      "line-11": {
        "id": "line-11",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "The consequences of this are not clear to me, but it doesn't look great -- generally, it seems that \"isolating the individual\" has not been good for either those individuals or their societies. And I don't think enough time or thought is being spent on what we want our social lives post-AGI to look like.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2103521027779420606_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2103521027779420606_1",
    "title": "There is a technical interview problem I like to ask which is so good, so cou...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2103521027779420606.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "There is a technical interview problem I like to ask which is so good, so counter-intuitive, the key insight so delightful, that one of my employees is bringing her husband to the office today just to try the problem.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Is he interviewing with you?",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "No! First time for everything.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2106980799262474528_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2106980799262474528_1",
    "title": "\"Coming of age\" books or movies used to be about turning 16 or 18.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2106980799262474528.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "\"Coming of age\" books or movies used to be about turning 16 or 18.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Now they're about turning 30.",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "Someone once said that life starts at 40 and everything else is research.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I'm pretty sure the number in that saying used to be 30.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2113382520498925767_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2113382520498925767_1",
    "title": "I'm noticing the growing possibility that Europe becomes very poor in the cou...",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2113382520498925767.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I'm noticing the growing possibility that Europe becomes very poor in the course of the next 10-20 years. You have the following factors:",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "1. Heavy industry totally uncompetitive against China, automakers etc. rapidly losing ground.",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "2. Services industry totally uncompetitive against AI.",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "3. No natural resources, or regulatory hurdles making their extraction impossible.",
        "next": "line-5"
      },
      "line-5": {
        "id": "line-5",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "4. No access to the new economy (no AI, no data centers, uncompetitive energy sector).",
        "next": "line-6"
      },
      "line-6": {
        "id": "line-6",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "5. Client states caught in one-way welfare ratchets, spend reallocation + investment well-nigh impossible.",
        "next": "line-7"
      },
      "line-7": {
        "id": "line-7",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "This seems under-contemplated.",
        "next": "line-8"
      },
      "line-8": {
        "id": "line-8",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "And we're talking really, seriously dirt poor: taken to its logical conclusion, many countries will have much, much smaller services and manufacturing industries -- economies may become much more heavily skewed toward natural resources and energy markets, where Europe has made it impossible for itself to compete.",
        "next": "line-9"
      },
      "line-9": {
        "id": "line-9",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "And I'm not saying that this is likely to happen, it's an extreme case. But the probability is greater than zero and appears to be growing.",
        "next": "line-10"
      },
      "line-10": {
        "id": "line-10",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "The EV of that is so negative that it's surprising to me that it's not coming up more.",
        "next": "line-11"
      },
      "line-11": {
        "id": "line-11",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "But what about tourism? Like, consider the Mediterranean waterfront as a natural resource.",
        "next": "line-12"
      },
      "line-12": {
        "id": "line-12",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Arguably the nicest Mediterranean weather in the world is in Cape Town, but South Africa is so far gone that they can no longer make productive use of it.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "tweet_2119820077491167242_1": {
    "id": "tweet_2119820077491167242_1",
    "title": "Let me tell you about renovations. Never start.",
    "source_directory": "source-tweets",
    "source_files": ["2119820077491167242.txt"],
    "start": "line-1",
    "nodes": {
      "line-1": {
        "id": "line-1",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Let me tell you about renovations. Never start.",
        "next": "line-2"
      },
      "line-2": {
        "id": "line-2",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Some people go crazy renovating their homes. After having done this for a few months, I understand why:",
        "next": "line-3"
      },
      "line-3": {
        "id": "line-3",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "First of all, it trains you to be hyperaware of errors. Your contractors are inevitably going to try to cut corners, and you want to both get your fair money's worth and have your vision executed, so you have to really pay attention, to things that normally you never would...",
        "next": "line-4"
      },
      "line-4": {
        "id": "line-4",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Was that scratch there before? Is this cabinet level?",
        "next": "line-5"
      },
      "line-5": {
        "id": "line-5",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Of course, once you're trained in this way, your hypervigilance extends to everything, even far outside your contractors' work: there's a half-inch gap between the doorframe and the floor? Sacrilege! Doesn't matter if it's been there for 40 years.",
        "next": "line-6"
      },
      "line-6": {
        "id": "line-6",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "A home is a complex thing with lots of detail, so inevitably, no matter where you look, the flaws will be endless.",
        "next": "line-7"
      },
      "line-7": {
        "id": "line-7",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Secondly, the other thing you learn is that whatever problems you see, you can fix them! Don't like it? Tear it out and do it again. If renting, you treat things as fixed -- but a house turns out to be shockingly malleable.",
        "next": "line-8"
      },
      "line-8": {
        "id": "line-8",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Literally everything can be changed. You can move lights, pipes, doors, tear out walls, there are no limits.",
        "next": "line-9"
      },
      "line-9": {
        "id": "line-9",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "These are the two core learnings of doing renovations, and combined, they are very dangerous: for people who are not used to saying \"good enough, whatever\", this becomes an endless perfectionist loop.",
        "next": "line-10"
      },
      "line-10": {
        "id": "line-10",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "I see. They'll have you changing stuff forever until you either run out of money or sanity.",
        "next": "line-11"
      },
      "line-11": {
        "id": "line-11",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Worse, you'll find that changing one thing often implies changing another thing...",
        "next": "line-12"
      },
      "line-12": {
        "id": "line-12",
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "I have a painting that looks like it's not level even though it is. Why? It's not aligned with the doorframe. Why? The doorframe itself isn't level. Why? The floor itself isn't level because it's 100 years old. But you can't live there while you're redoing the floors, of course.",
        "next": "line-13"
      },
      "line-13": {
        "id": "line-13",
        "speaker": "player",
        "text": "This is a scope-creep, yak-shaving classic: all you wanted was to hang your painting straight and now you live in a storage unit. Beware.",
        "end": true
      }
    }
  },
  "ambient_037_the_croissant_alibi": {
    "id": "ambient_037_the_croissant_alibi",
    "title": "The croissant alibi",
    "source_files": ["2024918834319425608.txt"],
    "tags": ["food", "work", "city"],
    "npc_voice": "Cheerfully caught in the act",
    "start": "start",
    "nodes": {
      "start": {
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Look at this bakery queue. Doesn't anyone work anymore? Yes, I'm in the queue. Yes, it is a weekday. How shall I explain myself?",
        "choices": [
          { "id": "start.choice-1", "text": "Your computer is compiling.", "next": "a" },
          { "id": "start.choice-2", "text": "You are allowed to take a break.", "next": "b" },
          { "id": "start.choice-3", "text": "I should get going.", "next": "leave" }
        ],
        "id": "start"
      },
      "a": {
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Excellent. A classic. What if my manager joins the queue?",
        "choices": [
          { "id": "a.choice-1", "text": "Ask what their computer is compiling.", "next": "a1" },
          { "id": "a.choice-2", "text": "Offer to bring back breakfast.", "next": "a2" }
        ],
        "id": "a"
      },
      "a1": {
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "An unexpected peer review. We'll conduct it over pastry.",
        "end": true,
        "id": "a1"
      },
      "a2": {
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "A practical pivot from suspicious absence to valued team member.",
        "end": true,
        "id": "a2"
      },
      "b": {
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "A dangerously humane explanation. What would make this a proper break?",
        "choices": [
          { "id": "b.choice-1", "text": "Stop checking your phone.", "next": "b1" },
          { "id": "b.choice-2", "text": "Actually enjoy the company.", "next": "b2" }
        ],
        "id": "b"
      },
      "b1": {
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "All right. I'll give my full professional attention to the croissant.",
        "end": true,
        "id": "b1"
      },
      "b2": {
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "Then hello. We've apparently been promoted from two people waiting to a conversation.",
        "end": true,
        "id": "b2"
      },
      "leave": {
        "speaker": "npc",
        "text": "May your pastry justify absolutely none of your life choices. It can just be good.",
        "end": true,
        "id": "leave"
      }
    }
  }
}
